        "original_id": "77df5ab9-f837-5821-a1fc-f2fdf6ea43ee",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sigmund Jähn, Christer Fuglesang, Darin\n- Roles: cosmonaut, pilot, physicist, ESA astronaut\n- Organizations: ESA, Soviet Union\n- Programs and Missions: Interkosmos programme, STS-116 Space Shuttle mission\n- Products: \"Breathing Your Love\" single\n- Places: Stockholm, space\n\nFacts:\n- Sigmund Werner Paul Jähn was born on 13 February 1937.\n- Christer Fuglesang was born on March 18, 1957 in Stockholm.\n- Sigmund Jähn is a German cosmonaut and pilot.\n- Christer Fuglesang is a Swedish physicist and an ESA astronaut.\n- In 1978, Sigmund Jähn became the first East German and the first German native to fly in space as part of the Soviet Union's Interkosmos programme.\n- On December 10, 2006, Christer Fuglesang launched aboard the STS-116 Space Shuttle mission at 01:47 GMT and became the first Swedish citizen in space.\n- In October 2009, Swedish astronaut Christer Fuglesang took two copies of the single \"Breathing Your Love\" into space because his daughter was a fan of Darin.\n- A photo of the disc with Earth in the distance was available on the official Darin website.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
